{%- comment -%}
  CARATFORUS — FIRST ACCESS
  ===========================================================================
  A conversion-first landing page for social and paid traffic. One job: say
  what is changing, and capture an email in a few seconds.

  SHOPIFY-NATIVE CAPTURE, NO BACKEND. The two signup forms are
  `{% form 'customer' %}` — the same mechanism the theme footer already uses,
  including its `contact[tags]` field. An email creates a Shopify CUSTOMER;
  interests become customer TAGS on that same record. There is no second
  database, no CRM, and no app route behind this page: nothing here needed
  one, so nothing here has one.

  WORKS WITHOUT JAVASCRIPT. The form posts natively and Shopify returns the
  page with `form.posted_successfully?` set, which renders the success panel
  below. `first-access.js` upgrades that to an in-place submit so a visitor
  arriving from an ad never watches a page reload — but the page is complete
  and converting before that file loads.

  NO COUNTDOWN, NO REFERRAL MECHANICS. "Launching Soon" is a statement, not a
  timer, and sharing is a courtesy with no codes, points or rewards attached.

  IMAGERY IS OPTIONAL AND OFF BY DEFAULT. Every image is a theme-editor
  setting with no default, so real brand photography can be dropped in
  without a code change — and the page is designed to stand up on typography
  alone until it is. Nothing here invents a product photograph.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'first-access.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<script>
  window.caratFirstAccessStrings = {
    copied: {{ 'templates.first_access.share.copied' | t | json }},
    shareText: {{ 'templates.first_access.share.text' | t | json }},
    submitting: {{ 'templates.first_access.form.submitting' | t | json }},
    error: {{ 'templates.first_access.form.error' | t | json }}
  };
</script>
<script src="{{ 'first-access.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{%- liquid
  assign t = 'templates.first_access'
  assign posted = false
  if section.settings.show_success_preview
    assign posted = true
  endif
-%}

<div class="carat-fa" data-carat-first-access>
  {%- comment -%} ------------------------------------------------ hero {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="carat-fa__hero" aria-labelledby="FirstAccessHeading">
    {%- if section.settings.hero_image != blank -%}
      <div class="carat-fa__hero-media" aria-hidden="true">
        {{
          section.settings.hero_image
          | image_url: width: 1600
          | image_tag:
            loading: 'eager',
            fetchpriority: 'high',
            sizes: '100vw',
            widths: '480, 768, 1100, 1600',
            class: 'carat-fa__hero-img'
        }}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="carat-fa__hero-inner">
      <p class="carat-fa__eyebrow">{{ 'templates.first_access.hero.eyebrow' | t }}</p>

      <h1 class="carat-fa__display" id="FirstAccessHeading">
        {{- 'templates.first_access.hero.heading' | t -}}
      </h1>

      <p class="carat-fa__lede">{{ 'templates.first_access.hero.lede' | t }}</p>

      {%- comment -%}
        The signup is part of the hero, not below it: a visitor from an ad
        must be able to convert without scrolling at all.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% render 'first-access-form',
        form_id: 'FirstAccessHero',
        section_id: section.id,
        posted: posted,
        compact: false
      %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} -------------------------------------------- the teasers

    Five, and deliberately short. Loose Diamonds is given the wide tile and
    carries the locked diamond message inside it rather than in a separate
    text-heavy section of its own.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="carat-fa__teasers" aria-labelledby="FirstAccessTeasers">
    <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="FirstAccessTeasers">
      {{- 'templates.first_access.teasers.a11y_heading' | t -}}
    </h2>

    <article class="carat-fa__tile carat-fa__tile--wide">
      <p class="carat-fa__tile-eyebrow">{{ 'templates.first_access.teasers.diamonds_label' | t }}</p>
      <h3 class="carat-fa__tile-heading">{{ 'templates.first_access.teasers.diamonds_heading' | t }}</h3>
      <p class="carat-fa__tile-text">{{ 'templates.first_access.teasers.diamonds_text' | t }}</p>

      <div class="carat-fa__diamond-message">
        <p class="carat-fa__diamond-claim">{{ 'templates.first_access.diamond.heading' | t }}</p>
        <p class="carat-fa__tile-text">{{ 'templates.first_access.diamond.promise' | t }}</p>
        <p class="carat-fa__diamond-no">{{ 'templates.first_access.diamond.no_pressure' | t }}</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="carat-fa__tile">
      <p class="carat-fa__tile-eyebrow">{{ 'templates.first_access.teasers.steals_label' | t }}</p>
      <h3 class="carat-fa__tile-heading">{{ 'templates.first_access.teasers.steals_heading' | t }}</h3>
    </article>

    <article class="carat-fa__tile">
      <p class="carat-fa__tile-eyebrow">{{ 'templates.first_access.teasers.group_label' | t }}</p>
      <h3 class="carat-fa__tile-heading">{{ 'templates.first_access.teasers.group_heading' | t }}</h3>
    </article>

    <article class="carat-fa__tile">
      <p class="carat-fa__tile-eyebrow">{{ 'templates.first_access.teasers.syos_label' | t }}</p>
      <h3 class="carat-fa__tile-heading">{{ 'templates.first_access.teasers.syos_heading' | t }}</h3>
    </article>

    <article class="carat-fa__tile">
      <p class="carat-fa__tile-eyebrow">{{ 'templates.first_access.teasers.custom_label' | t }}</p>
      <h3 class="carat-fa__tile-heading">{{ 'templates.first_access.teasers.custom_heading' | t }}</h3>
    </article>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} --------------------------------------------- disruption

    Short, premium, and about what the customer gets rather than about anyone
    else. No comparison table, and nothing said about any country's
    manufacturers.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="carat-fa__disruption" aria-labelledby="FirstAccessWhy">
    <h2 class="carat-fa__display carat-fa__display--sm" id="FirstAccessWhy">
      {{- 'templates.first_access.disruption.heading' | t -}}
    </h2>
    <p class="carat-fa__lede carat-fa__lede--center">
      {{- 'templates.first_access.disruption.body' | t -}}
    </p>
    <p class="carat-fa__us">{{ 'templates.first_access.disruption.us_based' | t }}</p>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ------------------------------------------- final signup

    The same form again so nobody has to scroll back up, with the launch-deal
    teaser kept to one line beside it rather than a second card section.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="carat-fa__closing" aria-labelledby="FirstAccessClosing">
    <h2 class="carat-fa__display carat-fa__display--sm" id="FirstAccessClosing">
      {{- 'templates.first_access.closing.heading' | t -}}
    </h2>
    <p class="carat-fa__lede carat-fa__lede--center">
      {{- 'templates.first_access.closing.body' | t -}}
    </p>

    {% render 'first-access-form',
      form_id: 'FirstAccessClosing',
      section_id: section.id,
      posted: posted,
      compact: true
    %}
  </section>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "First Access",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section section--first-access",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Imagery"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Optional. The page is designed to work without a photograph; add real brand photography here when it is ready."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "hero_image",
      "label": "Hero background image"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Preview"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_success_preview",
      "default": false,
      "label": "Preview the post-signup state",
      "info": "Theme editor only — shows the success and share panel so it can be styled. Turn off before publishing."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "First Access"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
